desc: Jezebel Drum Sequencer (Valley Topograph port) by chmaha
tags: midi generator sequencer drum pattern euclidean
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  A port of Valley Topograph (and its little sibling uGraph), Dale Johnson's take on the Mutable Instruments Grids
  topographic drum sequencer. Map X and Map Y move around a 5 x 5 map of drum patterns, the three Fill knobs set
  how busy each part is, and Chaos shakes the pattern a little more each bar. Three sequencer modes: Henri (Topograph's
  own, livelier blend of the map), Original (the Grids blend) and Euclidean (X, Y and Chaos set each part's length,
  the Fill knobs its number of hits).
  Jezebel makes MIDI only, so put a drum instrument after it on the same track. It follows REAPER's transport, or runs
  free on its own tempo knob with Topograph's swing. Accented hits play at the Accent velocity; the three extra
  outputs (accents, or accent, clock and reset) can go out as extra notes.
  Ported from Topograph and uGraph by Dale Johnson (Valley Audio, ValleyRackFree,
  https://github.com/ValleyAudio/ValleyRackFree, GPLv3+), based on Grids by Emilie Gillet (Mutable Instruments,
  https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack, GPLv3+).
  Title lettering: Zarathustra by Lorene Ceccon (SIL Open Font License 1.1), rendered into the panel image.
  Sidebar: Etoile polaire (The Pole Star), from La Lune et les etoiles (1902) by Alphonse Mucha, public domain
  (Bibliotheque nationale de France, Gallica btv1b90077190, via Wikimedia Commons). While the transport plays the
  picture comes gently to life; click it to switch the animation off or on.
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
